      "text": "Along the Mid-Atlantic Ridge, three hundred sixty atmospheres of crushing ocean weight trap superheated water as liquid. When robotic arms thrust a steel thermometer inside, that scalding fluid hits two-degree seawater\u2014freezing dissolved metals into towering black chimneys.",
